      "cfg:biomes/caves/desc": "The legacy of the Empire of Blood and Beast — rotting forest depths, underground menageries and ritual pits. The realm set out to make the perfect soldier by mixing the blood of men, beasts and magical creatures. First came mighty warriors, then packs, then a hunger that cannot be stopped. The underground laboratories became the lairs of cursed beastmen and mutated creatures.",
      "cfg:biomes/caves/name": "Lairs of Blood and Beast",
      "cfg:biomes/caves/tagline": "\"Perfect fusion destroys the self.\"",
      "cfg:biomes/crypt/desc": "The legacy of the Empire of the Dead Crown — catacombs, necropolises and imperial tombs. That realm feared oblivion above all else: its rulers poured their wealth into necromancy, into preserving bodies and raising immortal legions, so their dynasties might rule forever. Its mages learned to bring the dead back, but not to bring back the soul — whole cities became necropolises, and the eternal army became will-less undead.",
      "cfg:biomes/crypt/name": "Necropolis of the Dead Crown",
      "cfg:biomes/crypt/tagline": "\"Eternal life turns into eternal torment.\"",
      "cfg:biomes/dungeon/desc": "The legacy of the Empire of the Aetheric Archives — underground reactors, crystal towers, libraries of spells and machines that hold the aether in place. The realm staked everything on pure magical science, certain that magic could be measured, divided and stored as fuel. But magic proved to be a living force: the archives began to think for themselves, the machines slipped the leash, and the spells came into a will of their own.",
      "cfg:biomes/dungeon/name": "The Aetheric Archives",
      "cfg:biomes/dungeon/tagline": "\"Man became surplus to his own creation.\"",
      "cfg:biomes/labyrinth/desc": "The legacy of the Empire of the Rift — demons, cultists, warped architecture and portals to the lower planes. That realm went further than any other: its rulers tore rifts open, struck bargains with demons and called up things from beyond the edge of reality as weapons against the other realms. But the demons did not come to serve — they came to collect. The deepest levels already belong, in part, to another dimension.",
      "cfg:biomes/labyrinth/name": "The Rift Gates",
      "cfg:biomes/labyrinth/tagline": "\"You cannot be the master of an element — you are only its instrument.\"",
